# Falkensteinwand limestone (solid; M3): pale i faces with a wavy m bedding
# plane that wraps left/right (a cliff reads as continuous strata) and two
# short m joints. Open top: w lip (+ w flecks) with one small y/g/G grass
# tuft; open bottom (the Steinschlag overhang is mostly underside): a ragged
# d overhang edge with broken m shade and 1 px notches; open left m, open
# right d (light from the top left). Drawn by the pixel-artist with a
# throwaway script; the grids are the source.
# Autotiled (D-020): anim `auto`, frame = neighbour mask
# (1 = same tile above, 2 = right, 4 = below, 8 = left; level edge = same).
sprite = tile_kalkfels
size   = 16x16
origin = 0,0
anim   = auto frames=16 ticks=1
